(6770642, 1013731, 97225, '<td valign="top">It''s a lovely shot (with a bit of deja vu). However I didn''t see it as a seascape with a jetty, but as a jetty surrounded by sea.</td>', 'It''s a lovely shot (with a bit of deja vu). However I didn''t see it as a seascape with a jetty, but as a jetty surrounded by sea.', '2012-05-16 10:30:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(6770660, 1013710, 54645, '<td valign="top">Great title. Ha!</td>', 'Great title. Ha!', '2012-05-16 10:49:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6770673, 1014543, 69008, '<td valign="top">This was a good find.  I notice the way the "rays" of cracks in the glass work to draw me to the hole, and into the scene beyond.  This took some extra effort. I know that it''s not comfortable to set up and shoot to the rear from the inside of a car.  <br/>This scene might have worked better with an ultra wide or fisheye, using very small aperture for great DOF, and by getting less of the glass, like a frame, and a longer part of the horizon.  <br/>It''s different, and I see that I''m not the only one who likes that. Congrats on your new fish!</td>', 'This was a good find.  I notice the way the "rays" of cracks in the glass work to draw me to the hole, and into the scene beyond.  This took some extra effort. I know that it''s not comfortable to set up and shoot to the rear from the inside of a car.  This scene might have worked better with an ultra wide or fisheye, using very small aperture for great DOF, and by getting less of the glass, like a frame, and a longer part of the horizon.  It''s different, and I see that I''m not the only one who likes that. Congrats on your new fish!', '2012-05-16 11:09:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(6770677, 1014435, 145829, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tnun:</b></div><hr/><i> I am quite taken with this as more of a painting than a photo, so I don''t want it to sparkle.  It would be more of a pattern if you chopped the top off where the blue sky interrupts the clouds? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I actually tried that and found that it was a bit too flat, but I paint and tend to agree that this may make a great painting.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment.</td>', 'Originally posted by tnun: I am quite taken with this as more of a painting than a photo, so I don''t want it to sparkle.  It would be more of a pattern if you chopped the top off where the blue sky interrupts the clouds?   I actually tried that and found that it was a bit too flat, but I paint and tend to agree that this may make a great painting. Thanks for the comment.', '2012-05-16 11:17:44.000000', NULL, 0),
